this readme describes how elftombn.py work , it used to generated uboot.mbn  
during building the u-boot-single-image , 

elftombn.py call mbn_tools.py to generate mbn files ,
put these 2 file in same folder to make it work , you can find target scripts 
from chipcode QSDK-Base/meta-tools/scripts .

command to generate target openwrt-ipq807x-u-boot.mbn file from openwrt-ipq807x-u-boot.elf:
	python elftombn.py -f openwrt-ipq807x-u-boot.elf -o openwrt-ipq807x-u-boot.mbn

then , flash openwrt-ipq807x-u-boot.mbn to the uboot partiiton according to your DUT ,
for example , steps to upgrade only uboot partition for RAX120 : 
======================================
IPQ807x# setenv ipaddr 192.168.1.1 && setenv serverip 192.168.1.10
IPQ807x# tftpboot 0x42000000 openwrt-ipq807x-u-boot.mbn
IPQ807x# nand device 0 && nand erase 0x00d80000 0x00100000
IPQ807x# nand write $fileaddr 0x00d80000 $filesize
IPQ807x# reset
IPQ807x# delenv
IPQ807x# reset


the elf-to-mbn process flow contains following 3 steps :
1. pboot_gen_elf
2. image_header
3. pboot_add_hash

step 1 : generate hash table and phdr file .
xxx.elf --------> xxx_phdr.pbn , xxx.hash
	 pboot_gen_elf

step2 : generate the header of hash table
xxx_phdr.pbn , xxx.hash  -------->   xxx.hash.hd
			image_header

xxx_combined_hash.mbn = xxx.hash.hd + xxx.hash

xxx.hash.hd is a header file of xxx.hash, it use fixed size 0x28 .

step3 : generate mbn file 
xxx_phdr.pbn , xxx_combined_hash.mbn ---------> xxx.mbn
				     pboot_add_hash

use xxx_combined_hash.mbn replace the xxx_phdr.pbn from offset 0x10000

